From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] command: a borrowed image takes copy queue work, and a copy list without a fallback pool stays on its queue

A resource made over an image the embedder hands in (CreateResourceFromBorrowedHandle) never went
through image creation, so it was never marked compatible with the copy queue. A barrier or copy
on it in a COPY list asked for the compute fallback sequence, whose command pool an allocator only
makes when its queue is pure transfer and not concurrent; where the copy queue runs on a compute
or graphics family, or is a concurrent transfer queue, the pool is absent and recording asserted
on it, aborting the process. A borrowed image is marked compatible exactly when the device's copy
queue is concurrent, as the images vkd3d-proton makes over its image families are, and a COPY
list whose allocator has no fallback pool keeps the work on its own queue, which then can run it.
---
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/command.c b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
index df94418..a3864e3 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -2655,6 +2655,9 @@ static void d3d12_command_list_consider_new_sequence(struct d3d12_command_list *
 
 static void d3d12_command_list_copy_queue_fallback(struct d3d12_command_list *list)
 {
+    if (!list->allocator->fallback_pool.vk_command_pool)
+        return;
+
     if (!list->cmd.iterations[list->cmd.iteration_count - 1].fallback)
     {
         d3d12_command_list_end_transfer_batch(list);
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
index 8c95ca2..185eb5e 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
@@ -4167,6 +4167,9 @@ HRESULT d3d12_resource_create_borrowed(struct d3d12_device *device, const D3D12_
     if (!object->desc.MipLevels)
         object->desc.MipLevels = max_miplevel_count(desc);
 
+    if (device->concurrent_transfer_queue)
+        object->flags |= VKD3D_RESOURCE_COPY_QUEUE_COMPATIBLE;
+
     if (d3d12_device_supports_unified_layouts(device))
     {
         object->flags |= VKD3D_RESOURCE_GENERAL_LAYOUT;
